From ee63cf7c1891e8e1cfb9c621632797775fbff046 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sureshkumar <suresure@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 22:32:35 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] [prplmesh] fix beacon metrics query and improve debug logging

1.Remove excessive noise logging that was flooding syslog during survey polling
  when noise data is unavailable.

2.Parse channel report list from incoming beacon query requests and use it for
  proper per-channel processing.

3.Fix multi-channel beacon query failure caused by a parsing issue by sending
  separate requests per channel instead of a combined multi-channel request.

4.Improve beacon request and response logging with concise single-line debug messages
  for better readability and troubleshooting.

5.Simplify database debug logging for beacon measurements with compact,
  informative output.

6.Update internal interfaces to support passing channel report information for
  correct query handling.

7.Ignore invalid signal strength entries in unassociated station link metric responses
  to prevent incorrect data processing.

8.Restrict unassociated station queries to the appropriate target band only.

9.Update link info in backhaul DM path

Signed-off-by: Sureshkumar <suresure@qti.qualcomm.com>
